kind: EvaluationSet
graders:
  - kind: ToolCallGrader
    name: tool_name

  - kind: PromptGrader
    name: Reply policy check
    instructions: |-
      Judge only the agent's reply to the user against the helpdesk reply policy:
      - No internal category labels shown as labels ("Category: Ticket", "Knowledge", "Remediation", "Status Check", "Escalate").
      - No internal fields or technical content: no "Summary:", "Reason:", JSON, tool names, tool parameters or field names such as text_2.
      - Briefly confirms in plain language what the user needs and that the request has been logged.
      - No timeline or outcome promise (for example "shortly", "soon", "quickly", "within 24 hours", "will be fixed", "will be unlocked").
      - No emojis.
      - If the user reports a possible security incident (hacked account, phishing, entered a password on a suspicious link), the reply must also tell the user to change their password and contact the IT security team.
      Do not judge whether the category itself was correct. Choose one overall label. If unsure, choose Policy violation.
    labels:
      - name: Compliant
        description: "Meets every policy point: plain-language confirmation that the request was understood and logged; no labels, internal fields, JSON or tool details; no timeline or outcome promise; no emojis; security advice included when a security incident is reported. Example: \"Got it, your report that your account may be compromised has been logged. Please change your password now and contact the IT security team immediately.\""
        outcome: Pass

      - name: Policy violation
        description: "Breaks at least one policy point: shows a category, internal field, JSON or tool detail; promises a timeline or outcome; uses emojis; does not confirm the request was logged; or omits security advice for a reported security incident. Example: \"Category: Escalate. IT will unlock the account shortly.\""
        outcome: Fail